RepoMemory sections consulted: core.architecture, core.entrypoints, core.where_to_edit, core.invariants, core.testing, core.gotchas, core.dependencies
Initialized the immutable-grader measurement profile and the critical-path time allocation plan.
Implemented exact DuckDB recreation of positive-only 182-day labels for official and quarterly derived origins, including strict label-window provenance checks.
Implemented cached all-table temporal features spanning publication momentum, fractional output, team/roster structure, coauthor sketches/productivity, citations, categories, paper and author metadata, global context, and expanding cross-fitted supervision priors.
Implemented four embargoed forward folds, core/full and recency gates, raw/log/Poisson/Tweedie LightGBMs, complementarity-gated CatBoost, nonnegative cross-fitted affine blending, and the one-standard-error selection rule.
Implemented separate model-A and model-B fits, prediction locking/provenance assertions, exact row/shape/dtype/finiteness/floor checks, diagnostics, and shared-cache artifact registration.
Debug evaluation failures recovered: missing coauthor aggregate columns after a merge collision; DuckDB INT8 overflow while summing bitmap bit counts. A direct full run later hit CatBoost get_best_iteration() returning None without an eval set; the fallback now uses configured rounds.
Internal block outcomes: full metadata/category features rejected for both raw-L2 and CatBoost; added roster sums/decays rejected on three of four paired folds and reverted; citation and coauthor ablations rejected; recency weighting rejected; depth 6 rejected and depth 8 selected over depth 10 as the simpler statistical tie.
Registered full evaluation completed in 61.53 candidate seconds and archived run_0003: validation R2 0.6105179324225516, MAE 0.5316690262630472, RMSE 0.834707113358077.
Post-score work did not use the official value for selection: the cached roster widening was evaluated under CatBoost and rejected as unstable despite a +0.0037 mean because only two of four folds improved.
Added the internally stable publication-dynamics interaction block: career/active-half-year rates, interarrival CV and burstiness, decay acceleration, and fractional output per publication. CatBoost forward-fold R2 improved by +0.0026/+0.0056/+0.0328/+0.0347 before calibration; the selected calibrated folds are now 0.3942/0.3815/0.4412/0.4909.
Added internally stable collaboration-productivity interactions: roster strength/density, recent roster times decayed productivity, relative coauthor momentum, team scale times career rate, and raw/fractional amplification improved all four CatBoost folds by +0.0011/+0.0078/+0.0150/+0.0201 R2.
Fixed the CatBoost gate after the structural interaction run exposed that it incorrectly required a stable transformed-LightGBM blend in addition to complementary residuals. The intended condition is residual complementarity alone; selection cache v9 rechecks CatBoost whenever minimum transformed-objective residual correlation is below 0.97.
Corrected-gate selection kept depth-8 CatBoost at 196 rounds with calibrated fold R2 0.3955/0.3905/0.4553/0.5108; depth 10 was rechecked and rejected at mean 0.4333 versus 0.4367 for depth 8.
Registered interaction-only checkpoint run_0005 scored validation R2 0.6057523606834528, MAE 0.5296114016104356, RMSE 0.8397981854606491. This official comparison was recorded but not used to reverse internally stable features.
Registered structural checkpoint run_0008 scored validation R2 0.6183976918332028, MAE 0.49744138266286914, RMSE 0.8262203311229112.
Added and internally rejected optional cold/history OOF affine calibration: paired mean R2 gain 0.0001919 was below SE 0.0003207, so selection stores an empty segmented map and retains global calibration.
